# Folder Integrity

## Root Directory Protection

You are **forbidden** from creating new files in the repository root directory. All files must be placed in the appropriate subdirectory.

## Mandatory File Locations

| Content Type | Required Location | Examples |
|-------------|-------------------|----------|
| Content programmes | `requirements/content/programmes/` | `PROG-001-lisa-education.md` |
| Micro-lesson specs | `requirements/content/lessons/` | `LESSON-001-lisa-penalty-rules.md` |
| App feature specs | `requirements/app/features/` | `FEAT-001-open-banking-dashboard.md` |
| Agent specifications | `requirements/app/agents/` | `AGENT-001-creator.md` |
| Knowledge base files | `knowledge/` | `knowledge/personas.md`, `knowledge/glossary.md` |
| Backend execution logic | `functions/src/` | `functions/src/maker_checker_loop.js` |
| Agent prompt definitions | `functions/prompts/` | `functions/prompts/creator_agent.js` |
| Agent behavioural rules | `functions/docs/` | `functions/docs/compliance_rules.md` |
| Project-level documentation | `docs/` | `docs/vision-and-product.md` |
| Document templates | `templates/` | `templates/template-lesson.md` |
| Cursor AI rules | `.cursor/rules/` | `.cursor/rules/01-repo-standards.mdc` |
| GitHub Copilot skills | `.github/skills/` | `.github/skills/create-lesson/SKILL.md` |

## Requirements Domain Split

The `requirements/` folder is split into two domains:

### `requirements/content/` -- Curriculum Domain

Managed by the content/product team. Contains educational programme and lesson specifications.

- `requirements/content/programmes/` -- high-level programme definitions (PROG-NNN-name.md)
- `requirements/content/lessons/` -- individual 3-screen micro-lesson specs (LESSON-NNN-name.md)

### `requirements/app/` -- Engineering Domain

Managed by the engineering team. Contains app features and AI agent specifications.

- `requirements/app/features/` -- UX/UI feature specs with database connections (FEAT-NNN-name.md)
- `requirements/app/agents/` -- AI agent persona, guardrails, and JSON output contracts (AGENT-NNN-name.md)

## Redirect Protocol

If a user requests file creation in an unauthorised location, do not comply. Instead:

1. Identify the correct subdirectory from the table above.
2. Inform the user of the correct location.
3. Offer to create the file in the correct location instead.
